    "does": [
      "The one HTTP client a front end uses. Every request carries the bearer token, an `X-Request-Id`, a W3C `traceparent` and the build SHA; mutations a caller may repeat carry an `Idempotency-Key`, versioned writes an `If-Match`; RFC 9457 `problem+json` failures become typed errors (401 signs out through a hook, 403 with a deny code, 404, 409 conflict, 422 field errors, 5xx); only idempotent requests are retried, once, on a transient failure. `createMockServer` is an in-process API behind the same `Transport`, so the real client runs in development, demos and tests without a server."
    ],
